  "_comment_registers": "How the speaker wraps the command. One register per family (by a stable hash of its name); the wrapper's own words vary row to row. midfill puts a filler after the frame's first word; flat drops the frame's punctuation (an ASR transcript). Prefix registers that need an instruction to follow are never offered on a fronted arrangement.",

  "registers": {
    "bare":        {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "note", "q"], "wrap": "{X}"},
    "lead":        {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "note", "q"], "wrap": "{g_open} {X}"},
    "polite":      {"moods": ["imp"], "wrap": "{g_polite} {X}", "prefix": true},
    "polite_tail": {"moods": ["imp"], "wrap": "{g_polite} {X}{g_tail}", "prefix": true},
    "tail":        {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "note"], "wrap": "{X}{g_tail}"},
    "wake":        {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "q"], "wrap": "{wake} {X}"},
    "hedge":       {"moods": ["decl", "note"], "wrap": "{g_hedge} {X}", "prefix": true},
    "midfill":     {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "q"], "wrap": "{X}", "midfill": true},
    "flat":        {"moods": ["imp", "decl", "note", "q"], "wrap": "{X}", "flat": true}
  },

  "_comment_joiners": "Two-ask commands for the non-atomic diagnostic: {A} is an atomic family as written, {B} a second one with its slots renumbered. A compound is only ever built from constructions and a joiner on the SAME split.",

